# F-Droid index metadata for com.hrbons.fastlane.
# Sourced by ../rebuild-index.sh — plain shell assignments, no jq needed.
# NAME matches the launcher label (values/strings.xml app_name); the Dutch launcher name is
# "De Snelle Weg" (values-nl), but the index carries one name and the repo is English.
# The interface itself is Dutch — the SUMMARY says so, so nobody installs it expecting English.
#
# LICENSE is a deliberate choice, not inherited (2026-07-27, user: closed for good). The source
# repo is private and carries no LICENSE file, so "Proprietary" is the only factually true value,
# and the apps are meant to earn — MIT would hand everyone the right to rebuild this and ship it
# themselves. Proprietary -> MIT later is free; the reverse retracts a granted licence.
# (wordguesser is MIT because abons/wordguesser-src really is public, with a LICENSE file. That is
# the one exception and it stays that way; it is not the pattern for the others.)
NAME="Fast Lane"
SUMMARY="Life-simulation in the spirit of Jones in the Fast Lane - Dutch, tiny, native, offline"
DESCRIPTION="A tiny, native Android life-simulation in the spirit of Jones in the Fast Lane (Sierra, 1990). Walk a generated city - your flat, two schools, an employment office, two employers, a supermarket, a department store, a bank - and build up wealth, education, happiness and career within a limited number of weeks, against an AI rival that plays the same city by the same rules. Every week rotates: which vacancies are open, which school teaches, where the queues are, and how prices and wages move, so there is no single memorised route. Plus a seeded daily challenge that is the same city for everyone, statistics, a daily streak and earnable coins. Pure Kotlin on the Android framework only: no ads, no tracking, no third-party libraries. The interface is in Dutch."
LICENSE="Proprietary"
CATEGORIES='["Games"]'
